Spec: Feature WebAuthn Authentication and Management

Purpose:
  Implement WebAuthn (FIDO2) Relying Party in the Core Layer and a cross-platform desktop authentication flow in admin-frontend/mitm_fe_cpp using libfido2.

Platform: Rust/Axum, C++26/Qt6/libfido2

References:
  ../../../mitm-2.sdd
  ../../../core-layer/core-layer.sdd
  ../../../admin-frontend/mitm_fe_cpp/mitm_fe_cpp.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /core-layer/**
  /admin-frontend/mitm_fe_cpp/**
  /migrations/**

Must:
  All code documentation and comments must be in English.
  Every source file must include the standardized SPDX Apache-2.0 header.
  Database migration must extend admin_users with department and introduce webauthn_credentials.
  User registration must set is_active to false by default.
  Initial Bootstrap Admin via INITIAL_ADMIN_TOKEN must immediately have is_active set to true and ADMIN role.
  Provide WebAuthn RP endpoints (/api/v1/auth/webauthn/register/start, /finish, /login/start, /finish).
  Desktop frontend must prompt for Master Password first to decrypt config.enc.
  Desktop frontend must display interactive Login / Registration window only after config decryption.
  Desktop frontend must default LoginID to the current OS username.
  Desktop frontend must use libfido2 via Conan 2 for cross-platform FIDO2 operations.

Tasks:
  [ ] #1 Create database migration migrations/004_webauthn_and_department.sql.
  [ ] #2 Implement WebAuthn Relying Party in core-layer using webauthn-rs.
  [ ] #3 Update user registration in core-layer to set is_active to false, keeping bootstrap admin active.
  [ ] #4 Add libfido2 dependency to admin-frontend/mitm_fe_cpp via Conan 2 and CMakeLists.txt.
  [ ] #5 Refactor admin-frontend/mitm_fe_cpp startup flow to decrypt config first, then show Login/Registration UI.
  [ ] #6 Implement native Qt Login & Registration dialogs with libfido2 hardware key communication.
  [ ] #7 Update CHANGELOG.md in core-layer and admin-frontend/mitm_fe_cpp.

Done when:
  WebAuthn endpoints and frontend libfido2 registration/login flow succeed, user is created with is_active=false, and initial admin bootstrap remains active.
